 se adjudicó el 28 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 8 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 41 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.994 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no refleja actos ilícitos. Puede deberse a necesidades específicas o a precios de mercado. No implica que se haya partido ningún contrato ni que se haya actuado mal.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si en diciembre se repartieron otros contratos al límite. Analizar si los adjudicatarios repiten contratos en distintas fechas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 46 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 14.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.2 to 4.8. Contract [1], for 14,994 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: a pile-up of amounts just under the limit is a statistical indicator. It does not prove that any contract was broken up or that anyone acted improperly; it may reflect market prices, fixed budgets or separate needs.\nWhat can be checked: in the linked contract files, what was bought in each case and on which dates, and whether several contracts meet a single need that could have been procured at once.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"plantilla","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["Ope2BfpbZHc%2FbjW6njtWLw%3D%3D","sW4sCB7Kd8ysNfRW6APEDw%3D%3D","qoRtljt%2FzUnpxJFXpLZ%2B2A%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}